+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant with a time and a
+  zone; `qty` is a whole number) and answers `{ "tickets": 1, "dishes": 2 }`:
+  the tickets imported and their CSV rows, not counting skipped tickets. A
+  ticket that was already imported is skipped. If any row is invalid
+  (`bad_request`) or an item runs out (`not_enough_stock`), nothing is imported
+  and the message names the row; `row 2` is the first data row.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers, by item id and
+  for days in UTC (both inclusive), a list of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 0.3, "actual": 0.5, "difference": 0.2 }`.
+  `theoretical` is the use from sales, `actual` is every `consume` movement and
+  `difference` is actual minus theoretical. Items with no use are left out.
